\"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"216\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"221\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(FCC2-VDDA-Pad21)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If these pins are truly unconnected, the FCC MCU receives no core or analogue supply and cannot run. The same pattern appears on NAVC2 VDD pins, so it may be an export artefact rather than a board fault, which is why confidence is low.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The PCA9685 PWM driver has its A0 address pin tied to +3.3V instead of GND, which shifts its I2C address from the specified 0x40 to 0x41. A lower-confidence concern is that the FCC MCU's VDD/VDDA/VBAT pins appear unconnected in the netlist.\"\n}",
